    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d703">

                <pb facs="0808" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg696"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/1445</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 97</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-11-20">November 20, 1935</date>.<lb/>[Received December
                        19.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the Embassy’s
                    despatch No. 63 of October 31, 1935,<anchor n="19" xml:id="d703-f1"/> regarding
                    the conflict between the Chinese and Japanese authorities at Swatow, and to
                    enclose for the information of the Department a copy of despatch No. 90 of
                    November 6, 1935, from the Consulate at Swatow<anchor n="20" xml:id="d703-f2"/>
                    reporting on the present status of Sino-Japanese relations at that place. It
                    will be observed from that despatch that potentialities for future trouble there
                    apparently still exist.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. P.
                            Lockhart</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of
                        Embassy</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d703-f1" n="19" xml:id="d703-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see telegram No. 69, October 17, 3 p.m., from the Counselor of
